From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 209] panvk/csf: apply the translation-layer write rule to DXVK too
Generated-by: LLM

DXVK flushes one barrier per batch of resource accesses whose destination
scope names every usage each resource allows, writes included, so a later
shader write never relies on the execution dependency of a barrier whose
destination scope only reads.  Treat the "DXVK" engine like "vkd3d" for
the deferred-wait write rule, and log the detected engine and the rule in
use once.  A biblioklept who checks the lending rules of both libraries
before skipping the queue.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/208

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
index 32998959..9c680ae6 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_cmd_buffer.h
@@ -1123,10 +1123,12 @@ enum panvk_lazy_vt_flush_reason {
 void panvk_per_arch(cmd_lazy_flush)(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf,
                                    enum panvk_subqueue_id subqueue,
                                    enum panvk_lazy_vt_flush_reason reason);
-/* Whether vkd3d-proton drives the device: D3D12 requires an explicit
- * transition between reads and later writes of a resource, so a compute or
- * vertex shader write never relies on an earlier image transition's
- * execution dependency. */
+/* Whether vkd3d-proton or DXVK drives the device.  Both put write access
+ * in the destination scope of any barrier that orders reads before later
+ * writes of a resource (vkd3d-proton: D3D12 requires an explicit transition
+ * to a write state; DXVK: a flushed access barrier names every usage the
+ * resource allows, writes included), so a shader write never relies on the
+ * execution dependency of a barrier whose destination scope only reads. */
 bool panvk_per_arch(cmd_d3d12_semantics)(const struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf);
 
 static inline void
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
index 9732d556..68f8850c 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -572,9 +572,10 @@ collect_cache_flush_info(enum panvk_subqueue_id subqueue,
  * next draw or dispatch on that subqueue whose shaders read images or write
  * memory, before geometry/tessellation/gpu_prerast draws and internal
  * compute work, before events, meta operations and secondary execution,
- * and at the end of the command buffer.  Under vkd3d-proton, D3D12 requires
- * an explicit transition between reads and later writes of a resource, so
- * shader writes do not need the deferred wait there.  Transfer and query
+ * and at the end of the command buffer.  Under vkd3d-proton and DXVK any
+ * barrier that orders reads before later writes has write access in its
+ * destination scope (see cmd_d3d12_semantics), so shader writes do not need
+ * the deferred wait there.  Transfer and query
  * work never observes those image writes.  A later barrier that makes
  * another subqueue wait for a subqueue with a deferred wait hands the
  * deferred wait over when its part of that barrier only reads, and emits
@@ -632,7 +633,9 @@ panvk_per_arch(cmd_d3d12_semantics)(const struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
       const struct vk_instance *instance =
          cmdbuf->vk.base.device->physical->instance;
       const char *engine = instance->app_info.engine_name;
-      d3d12 = engine && !strcmp(engine, "vkd3d");
+      d3d12 = engine && (!strcmp(engine, "vkd3d") || !strcmp(engine, "DXVK"));
+      mesa_logi("panvk: engine '%s': %s barrier write rules", engine ? engine : "",
+                d3d12 ? "D3D translation-layer" : "strict Vulkan");
    }
    return d3d12;
 }
